      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could the message name the change this covers? As far as I can see, the anonymous cases check the copy in aosp/4367981, which I\u0027ve asked to drop (see my comment there), so they would fail with the `-EINVAL` kept. The private file case would still apply: `copy_vma()` carries a file VMA\u0027s slice, so no copy is needed. Could the test keep just that case, with a message along these lines?\n\n```\nCheck that a private file mapping of a 4KB process keeps its contents\nand file offsets when mremap() moves it to another slice of a native\npage, and that a COW write after fork() doesn\u0027t reach sibling slices.\n```",
