      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T18:28:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The private file case is a nice addition. As far as I can see, though, it can\u0027t notice a wrong file offset after the move: the memfd holds `0x20` everywhere, and every slice is dirtied before `mremap()`, so all four PTEs are anonymous COW pages. aosp/4367981 also carries the source slice through `copy_vma()` so that a moved file VMA keeps its file offset.\n\nWould it be worth writing a different byte into each 4KB slice of the memfd, dropping one slice with `MADV_DONTNEED` after the move, and checking that it faults back in with its own file byte?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "a056840050cbc6c10c5776160f9e585d7fa02894",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
